Behaviours:
- Where an icon stands for one specific model, a GPT model shows the OpenAI logo (black or white per theme, as the Codex provider does) instead of its provider's logo. This covers GPT models a Claude instance lists through the fleet proxy (slugs such as claude-fable-5-dd-los-2.6-tpg, names such as "GPT 6.2 Sol") and GPT models of any other provider.
- Places: model picker rows (provider tabs and Favorites), the composer's model picker trigger (single and multiple selection), the composer's model mention menu and model mention chips (their accent follows the logo), the current-provider icon of sidebar thread rows and their hover card, thread chip hover cards, handoff endpoints in the timeline (icon and label colour), subagent hover cards, the provider subagent bar, the guest page's model label and the usage model dialog header.
- A model is GPT when its display name starts with "GPT" followed by a space, a dash or a digit (any case), or its slug starts with "gpt-". One helper decides it: modelBrandDriverKind(driverKind, model) in providerIconUtils returns the codex driver kind for a GPT model and the provider's own driver kind otherwise.
- Custom OpenAI-compatible endpoints keep their initials tile, which already carries the OpenAI mark.
- Provider-level icons (picker sidebar tabs, settings cards, usage charts, subagent avatars, the sidebar's earlier-provider icons, command palette harness icons) keep the provider's logo. Instance badges (accent colour, initials) are unchanged.
- No server or contracts change.

